or every existing invocation, including `--json`, `--no-recommend-phases` and `--help`. |\n| REQ-003 | The quiet line and the report's level line are emitted from one shared format site, so a change to one cannot leave the other behind. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--quiet --json` prints the unchanged JSON document; when both flags are present, `--json` takes precedence over `--quiet`. |\n| REQ-005 | Error paths are unchanged: missing `--loc`/`--files`, non-numeric values and unknown options still exit 1 with the same message on stderr, even when `--quiet` is present. |\n| REQ-006 | stderr behavior is unchanged under `--quiet`; the flag suppresses report lines on stdout only. |\n| REQ-007 | `--quiet` appears in the header OPTIONS comment and in `show_help()` output. |\n| REQ-008 | `--quiet` is order-independent and composes with `--recommend-phases`, `--no-recommend-phases` and `--phase-threshold` without error. |\n| REQ-009 | Exit codes are unchanged: 0 on success, 1 on any usage or input error. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db | wc -l` prints `1`, the line reads `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`, and the exit code is 0.\n- **SC-002**: The default output for a fixed invocation is byte-identical before and after the change — the `diff` of the two captures is empty.\n- **SC-003**: `--quiet --json` output equals `--json` output for the same inputs — the `diff` of the two captures is empty.\n\n**Given** the script runs with `--quiet --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db`, **When** it exits, **Then** stdout is exactly the single line `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)` and the exit code is 0.\n\n**Given** the same invocation without `--quiet`, **When** it exits, **Then** stdout equals the pre-change multi-line report byte-for-byte.\n\n**Given** `--quiet --json --loc 100 --files 3`, **When** it exits, **Then** stdout is the same JSON document `--json` alone prints.\n\n**Given** `--quiet` with neither `--loc` nor `--files`, **When** it runs, **Then** it exits 1, the missing-input error goes to stderr, and stdout is empty.\n\n**Given** `--quiet --bogus`, **When** it runs, **Then** it exits 1 with the unknown-option error on stderr.\n\n**Given** `--help` with or without `--quiet`, **When** it runs, **Then** the help text names `--quiet` and exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bash` and coreutils already required by the script | None — no new dependency | The flag is pure bash; nothing is installed |\n| Dependency | Downstream readers of the `Recommended Level:` label | A renamed label breaks them | Reuse the exact existing string through one shared format site and pin it with a byte comparison in verification |\n| Risk | The quiet line and the report line drift apart in a later edit | Med | Both call one helper, so there is a single literal to change; verification diffs the quiet line against the report's line |\n| Risk | `--quiet` hides phase guidance a caller still needs | Low | The flag is opt-in; the default report and `--json` remain for richer reads |\n| Risk | An argument-parser edit regresses an existing flag | Med | Byte-diff the default and JSON outputs against a captured baseline, and run every existing flag in the matrix |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: `--quiet` adds no measurable runtime — the scoring path is unchanged and only the output selection differs; the script still completes in the same tens of milliseconds.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: `--quiet` takes no value, so it adds no input-parsing or injection surface; the script performs no authentication and reads no credential.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: The exit-code contract is unchanged: 0 on success, 1 on any usage or input error, with errors on stderr only.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: `--quiet` alone still fails the required-input check (`--loc` or `--files`), exiting 1 with the error on stderr and nothing on stdout.\n- Maximum input: extreme values such as `--loc 100000 --files 999 --quiet` still print exactly one line; there is no buffering or truncation path.\n- Flag position: `--quiet` works anywhere in the argument list, matching the script's existing order-independent parse loop.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: N/A — the script is fully offline and calls no service.\n- Network timeout: N/A — the script makes no network request.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: N/A — the script is single-shot and keeps no intermediate state.\n- Session expiry: N/A — the script has no session concept.\n- Output-channel separation: errors never reach stdout, so a caller capturing stdout under `--quiet` cannot capture an error line by accident.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 4/25 | Files: 1, LOC: ~15, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 2/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N — additive flag, default output preserved |\n| Research | 2/20 | The script was read end-to-end; no investigation remains |\n| Multi-Agent | 0/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 2/15 | Dependencies: 1 (readers of the level label) |\n| **Total** | **10/100** | **Level 3** (declared by the authoring dispatch; measured complexity is low, so the packet keeps its scaffolded Level 3 contract) |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | The quiet line and the report's level line diverge in a later edit | M | M | One shared format site; verification diffs the quiet output against the report's level line |\n| R-002 | `--quiet` hides phase guidance a caller needs | L | L | Opt-in flag; the default report and `--json` remain for richer reads |\n| R-003 | An argument-parser edit regresses an existing flag | M | L | Byte-diff the default and JSON outputs against the captured baseline; run the full flag matrix |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: Scripted caller reads the level in one line (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** dispatch harness, **I want** a `--quiet` flag that prints only the recommended-level line, **so that** I can capture the level directly instead of grepping a multi-line report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Human keeps the familiar report (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** human operator, **I want** the default output to stay exactly as it is, **so that** the report I read today is unchanged by the new flag.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-003: JSON consumer keeps a stable document (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** scripted `--json` caller, **I want** JSON output to be unaffected when `--quiet` is also passed, **so that** my schema assumptions hold for every flag combination.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does `--quiet` change `--json` output? No — JSON is already a single machine-readable document, so it wins when both flags are present.\n- Does `--quiet` suppress stderr or skip phase scoring? No — stderr is unchanged and scoring still runs; the flag only selects a shorter stdout path.\n- Does the quiet line keep the `Recommended Level:` label instead of a bare number? Yes — the label is the existing contract, and a bare value would be a second format to maintain.\n- None blocking.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: ADR-001 in `plan.md` §L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n---\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
